# Why this file exists
#
# Git does not track empty folders — only files.
# If this folder has no files, Git ignores it completely.
# When someone clones the repo, benchmarks/results/ would not exist.
# benchmark.sh tries to save CSV files here — it would error if the folder is missing.
#
# Solution: put one empty file here so Git tracks the folder.
# This file is named .gitkeep by convention — it signals to anyone
# reading the repo that this file's only job is to keep the folder alive in Git.
#
# The actual CSV files generated by Locust are gitignored (see .gitignore).
# Only this placeholder file is committed.